 "capsule": "Yan (燕) was one of the Seven Warring States of Zhou-era China, a hereditary fief traced to the Duke of Shao, Ji Shi, a royal kinsman of King Wu of Zhou, centered on its capital Ji (near modern Beijing) in the far northeast. During the Warring States period it ranked among the seven great powers, expanding along the Liaoning corridor after General Qin Kai's campaigns against the Donghu, though the 227 BC assassination attempt on the future Qin Shi Huang, sent by Crown Prince Dan, provoked Qin's final conquest, with Ji falling in 226 BC and the remnant state extinguished in 222 BC. This ancient Yan is unrelated to the Xianbei-ruled Former Yan founded over five centuries later by the Murong clan.",
